From afb59f5e8cb88f876e6286030a8c988fa986be7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:01:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - carry the final CTR counter wrap into the
 returned IV

The engine increments only the low 32 bits of its AES-CTR counter. The
existing split handles wrapping inside a request, but not wrapping just
after the final block: no split is needed to produce correct ciphertext,
yet the saved state still lacks the carry into the high 96 bits.

Propagate that carry when copying the completed ordinary CTR IV back to
the caller. An all-ones IV with a one-block or shorter message must return
zero, and a counter starting at fffffffe must carry after two blocks,
including a partial last block. Keep the existing internal-wrap split and
the RFC3686/authenc completion behavior.

With size-based fallback disabled, the device matrix reported 198 such IV
mismatches while ciphertext checks passed. A software driver model with a
32-bit hardware counter reproduces the exact failing cases. The fix passes
all 3564 CTR repetitions, 6336 skcipher cases and 12824 authenc cases in
QEMU TCG, including both directions and partial blocks. Physical device
validation remains required.

Signed-off-by: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 eip93-common.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/eip93-common.c b/eip93-common.c
index b605c33..1a9eb92 100644
--- a/eip93-common.c
+++ b/eip93-common.c
@@ -908,8 +908,17 @@ void eip93_handle_result(struct eip93_device *eip93, struct eip93_cipher_reqctx
 				 sizeof(*rctx->sa_state),
 				 DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 
-	if (!IS_ECB(rctx->flags))
+	if (!IS_ECB(rctx->flags)) {
 		memcpy(reqiv, rctx->sa_state->state_iv, rctx->ivsize);
+		/*
+		 * The engine increments only the low 32 counter bits. A wrap
+		 * on the last block needs no split, but still needs its carry
+		 * in the returned IV for the next ordinary CTR request.
+		 */
+		if (IS_CTR(rctx->flags) && !IS_RFC3686(rctx->flags) &&
+		    !rctx->authsize && !rctx->sa_state->state_iv[3])
+			crypto_inc(reqiv, AES_BLOCK_SIZE - sizeof(u32));
+	}
 
 	kfree(rctx->sa_state_ctr);
 	kfree(rctx->sa_state);
-- 
